    feat(hybrid): Andes V5 CSR transport, minimal (mxstatus round-trip)

    Prototype the Andes V5 CSR block via a single scalar, mxstatus (0x7C4),
    gated on HYBRID_FLAG_ANDES. ResumeDriver::restore_andes_m_ext tolerant-writes
    mxstatus so a core without the CSR mirrors it as a no-op, and
    StateDrain::drain_andes_m_ext re-reads it into state.andes.mxstatus so an
    in-ROI write reaches the drained state instead of the stale QEMU1 passthrough.
    This is the minimal slice: only mxstatus, hand-coded, with no caps gating
    (unconditional tolerant write); PMA plus the other twelve scalars via the
    X-macro sweep are the completion. Tests reduce the Andes-block cases to assert
    mxstatus round-trips and that no Andes write/re-read fires without the flag.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

